comments.body:
@pcbeingused333 I appreciate you filing bugs and opening PRs, but I also want to set some expectations:

1. NeMo Agent Toolkit is currently deprecated and will be end-of-life at the end of the calendar year. This effectively means that only critical bugs and corresponding fixes should be opened.
2. If you do choose to commit, please note that the work that you sign off on is yours, even if you have an agent do it (which most definitely appears to be the case). I would prefer **few** high-quality fixes over **many** low-quality/effort fixes.
